The Fremennik warband are the weakest monsters in the Colosseum, but can quickly overwhelm new players. Similarly to the [[Jal-Nib]]s from the Inferno, the warband will spawn in the centre of the arena, though unlike the nibs, they will immediately dart towards the player upon spawning. Despite the archer and seer using ranged weapons, the trio will only attack upon reaching '''melee range''' of the player. Upon reaching the player, the trio will begin attacking on different ticks, starting with melee, magic then ranged. The warband will position themselves accordingly, provided that there is space for them to stand there; the berserker will prioritise standing north of the player, the seer to their east and the ranger to the west. If these tiles are blocked by an obstacle they will attack from a different position, but the attack rotation is still the same.

If players use a hit and run tactic on the frems to avoid having them hit, this may cause their attack sequence to stagger with some members skipping attacks, such as the seer attacking first instead of the berserker. Learners frequently sabotage themselves by doing this, as it is important to kill them as quickly as possible, especially if other enemies have sight of the player, which can likely prove fatal.

If the '''Quartet''' handicap is active, a fourth member will spawn to the south, creating a diamond-like formation. This fourth member will attack on the same tick as its fellow.

Despite their weapons, their combat stats are identical; 50 hitpoints (48 for the Berserker), with an Attack, Strength, Ranged, and Magic level of 110, and 80 Defence. The seer has a max hit of 12, the archer has a max hit of 14 and the berserker has a max hit of 29. The trio are very accurate regardless of the player's defensive gear, so it is necessary to kill them once it is safe to do so to minimise damage taken.

When using a combat style corresponding to their weakness, the player's attacks will always hit and for a [[maximum hit]]. The only exception is [[Ice Barrage]] on the berserker; a minimum magic attack bonus of +104 and [[Augury]] is needed to guarantee a freeze on it and the other frems. The table below shows the strongest options for each NPC.

