[[File:Manticore.png|left|56x56px]]
[[Manticore]]s are another dangerous enemy in the Colosseum. Unlike other monsters, the Manticore will charge up a three-hit attack which takes 10 ticks to complete. Similarly to colossi, the manticore has an attack range of 15. The attack arrangement is dependent on spawn, and it will utilise a magic-ranged or ranged-magic as the first two attacks in sequence; the third attack is always melee. The magic attack is a bright blue orb, the ranged attack is a green arrowhead, and the melee attack is an orange spiky ball. These attacks are launched one tick after each other, followed by a 7-tick lull while the Manticore recharges. The melee and magic orbs deal up to 31 damage, while the ranged orb deals up to 36 instead. This can deal a total of 98 damage if all three hits land as maximum hits; although such a scenario is unlikely, the rapid attacks can overwhelm a player if not properly prepared.

Because of this, manticores can be potentially dangerous when paired with colossi, such as a manticore stacked alongside a ranger and shocker, as it is impossible to flick against all three.

'''Beware:''' Despite their visual similarity to the [[The Leviathan|The Leviathan's]] projectile attacks, '''you must pray accordingly against projectiles before they are launched''', as opposed to being able to pray against the projectiles while they are mid-flight.

The '''Mantimayhem 1''' modifier changes the Manticores damage output, causing 2 attacks per style for a total of 6, but not changing how you would handle prayer flicking them. These attacks roll separate accuracy checks and damage. While harmless if the player can flick their attacks, they will be severely punished if they fail to do so, as each set of orbs can deal up to 62/72 damage and cause an even quicker death.

The '''Mantimayhem 2''' modifier causes the Manticores attacks to inflict [[venom]] upon an unprotected hit, though it clears at the end of the wave. With this modifier, a [[sanfew serum]] is necessary to avoid taking unnecessary damage while clearing a wave, especially if envenomed early. Other forms of venom curing are generally unhelpful due to the nature of the fight.

The '''Mantimayhem 3''' modifier will unlock any pattern of the manticore's attacks, allowing for attack patterns such as Melee-Mage-Ranged, Ranged-Melee-Mage, etc. This can adversely affect the way pillar solves work and makes them extremely dangerous due to their increased damage and venoming capabilities. 

In wave 9, 10 and 11, two manticores will appear. When one of these manticores has sight of the player, the other manticore that is within 15 tiles of them and also having sight on the player will copy the pattern of the first one. If the first manticore is killed before that happens, the second one will pick a random attack pattern. This can be used to manipulate their first or second attack to handle pillar solves depending on what else is behind them. When two manticores have sight of the player and are able to attack them, one manticore will dump its attacks on the player, and 5 ticks after that, the second manticore will do so, resulting in their attack speed effectively being reduced to 15 ticks.

'''Warning: It is possible for two manticores to attack in rapid succession and ignore the 5 tick delay if the player hides from one's line of sight and then pops out while the other is attacking. The manticores will not stagger their attack speed if this occurs, and can result in swift death if unprepared.'''

